# First failure on this commit (kept as evidence, not edited): CI run 37857587058, job 113585384307 (p19-report-v2-20),
# commit e39268e4. 19 of 20 cases PASS; P19R_BROWSER_MOBILE_REPORT stopped at assert.ok(doc&&doc.id===last.publication_id).
# The same suite passed 20/20 on 976f4c43, 9112f3ed and 05b2368f. Cause: a test-script race, not the product. The screen
# draws the report article only after erp_cp7_read_report_v2 answered with the same id as the finished request
# (src/NativeStagedReportsPanel.tsx `open`: a different id throws 'Identitas laporan server berubah.'), and the run
# shows no console error. The script's response listener pushed a reply only after its body had been read
# (`await r.json()`), so the article could be visible before the read reply was recorded. Fix: each reply is recorded
# when it arrives (arrival order) and its body awaited before any assertion reads it; the script also waits until the
# read reply is recorded. Every check is unchanged (one unit per step, DONE with a publication, same id, finance
# DEFERRED/INCLUDED, freshness, section read with the access epoch, no v1 call). The K3 browser journey had the same
# listener pattern and gets the same fix. No product code changed.
